let VERSION = "0.1.0"

fn usage() -> String = """
  nautra — build, ship and run WebAssembly workloads

  Usage: nautra <command> [options]

    run [grants] IMAGE|FILE.wasm [args…]   run a workload with exactly what you grant it
    build [-t NAME] [-f Nautrafile] [PATH]  package a .wasm file as an image
    images                                  list stored images
    inspect IMAGE|FILE.wasm                 what an image is, what it asks for, what it can reach
    tag SOURCE NAME                         give a stored image another name
    rmi IMAGE…                              remove stored images
    pull IMAGE                              fetch an image from an OCI registry
    push IMAGE                              publish an image to an OCI registry
    version                                 print the version

  A workload starts with nothing: no directory, no network, no environment,
  a closed stdin. Each grant on `run` opens one thing:

    -v, --volume HOST:GUEST[:ro]   a directory, where the guest sees it
    -e, --env NAME=VALUE | NAME    a variable; a bare NAME copies the host's
        --allow-net HOST:PORT      one destination; HOST, *:PORT, or * for all
    -p, --publish [ADDRESS:]PORT   serve an HTTP component there (this machine only by default)
    -i, --interactive              this terminal's stdin
    -m, --memory SIZE              a memory ceiling (64m, 1g)
        --timeout DURATION         a deadline (500ms, 30s, 2m)
        --fuel N                   a ceiling on executed instructions

  Grants come before the image; everything after it is the workload's own.

  An image is named [REGISTRY/]NAME[:TAG][@DIGEST]. A name with no registry is
  local. Images live in $NAUTRA_HOME (default ~/.nautra). Registry logins are
  read from NAUTRA_USERNAME and NAUTRA_PASSWORD.
  """
